# Module Hub Redesign Assessment

## Progress Checklist
- [x] Navigate to dashboard and click a module card (Used ID 19 as 17/18 failed)
- [x] Explore Overview tab & capture screenshot
- [x] Explore Assignments tab & capture screenshot
- [x] Explore Module Brief tab & capture screenshot
- [x] Summarize strengths and weaknesses

## Findings
- Overview: Shows assignment status summary and module details (description, credits, workload). The layout is somewhat sparse with large cards for single stats.
- Assignments: List view with checkboxes/icons for status. Clean but simple.
- Module Brief: Includes "Extracted Schedule" (which remains in loading state), Knowledge Base upload, and an AI Assistant.
- General Layout: Side navigation, top header with module info, and tabbed content below.

## Strengths
- Minimalist and clean aesthetic.
- Functional tab navigation.
- Useful AI assistant integration.

## Weaknesses
- Robustness: IDs 17 and 18 return 500 errors, showing the site is sensitive to data issues.
- Empty states: "Extracted Schedule" shows a perpetual loading state if data is missing.
- Information Density: "Assignment Status" cards are very large for the amount of info they convey.
- Discoverability: The "Back to Courses" link is small.
